_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-122338" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "v(x)={x}^{2}+x+2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9200e531b3ab7444cb5a4c08c9cf15199728fb4376cbd0f00077184e7aa70d" "basis" 1577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-122338" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "v(x)=\\sqrt{2({x}^{2}+x+6)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9200e531b3ab7444cb5a4c08c9cf15199728fb4376cbd0f00077184e7aa70d" "basis" 1577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-122316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis in the direction of increasing $x$ where $x\\ge 0.$ When the displacement of $P$ from the origin $O$ is $x$ meters, the velocity is given by $v(x)=\\frac{1}{(1+x)^{2}}\\,m/s.$ Initially, $P$ is at the origin $O.$ Find $x$ as a function of time $t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9200e531b3ab7444cb5a4c08c9cf15199728fb4376cbd0f00077184e7aa70d" "basis" 1577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-122316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/assets/2093298b6cacb0b29f874d401ccca40560517ff5887763e9a2b88bf4bc051abb.png)\n\nWe're given that the velocity function $v(x)$ is\n\n$$\nv(x)=\\frac{1}{(1+x)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWe know that $v=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$ Therefore, we have the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{(1+x)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSeparating the variables and integrating both sides with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{1}{(1+x)^{2}} \\\\ (1+x)^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =1 \\\\ \\int (1+x)^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int \\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int (1+x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}(1+x)^{3} & =t+K \\\\ (1+x)^{3} & =3t+C \\\\ 1+x & =\\sqrt[3]{3t+C} \\\\ x & =\\sqrt[3]{3t+C}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $x=0$ when $t=0.$ Therefore, $C=1,$ and the particular solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\sqrt[3]{3t+1}-1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9200e531b3ab7444cb5a4c08c9cf15199728fb4376cbd0f00077184e7aa70d" "basis" 1577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-122316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "785f7610edd208db81cfb7c4ec13a140b5ce47e04ba0e053de3c67f7552cdd94" "basis" 1577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-122316" "field" "selection" "a